Usage: openbuff [options] [prompt...]

Local/BYOK AI coding assistant

Arguments:
  prompt                        Initial prompt to send to the agent

Options:
  -v, --version                 Print the CLI version
  --agent <agent-id>            Run a specific agent id (skips loading local
                                .agents overrides)
  --clear-logs                  Remove any existing CLI log files before
                                starting
  --continue [conversation-id]  Continue from a previous conversation
                                (optionally specify a conversation id)
  --cwd <directory>             Set the working directory (default: current
                                directory)
  --plan                        Start in PLAN mode
  --local                       Local/BYOK mode (default; kept for
                                compatibility)
  --trust-project-agents        Allow executable agents and MCP config from this
                                project or its parent directory
  --attach                      Attach to a running `openbuff serve` over ACP
                                instead of running in-process
  --serve-socket <path>         Unix socket of a running `openbuff serve` (used
                                with --attach; or OPENBUFF_SERVE_SOCKET)
  --serve-token <token>         Auth token for --serve-socket (or
                                OPENBUFF_SERVE_TOKEN)
  -h, --help                    Show this help message

Commands:
  init                 Create local project context: openbuff init
  run                  Headless agent: openbuff run --timeout 60 "check changes"
  replay               Read recorded evidence: openbuff replay <run-id> --from-step 2
  dash                 Browse local journals: openbuff dash [--export <directory>]
  serve                Serve a local agent session: openbuff serve --help
  mcp                  Serve local tools over MCP: openbuff mcp --help

Use openbuff <command> --help for options.
Wrapper actions: openbuff --check-update checks registry freshness; openbuff --update installs a verified update.
In chat: /help opens the slash command directory; /provider configures BYOK routing.
